  "transcript_segments": [
    {
      "start": 11.94,
      "end": 17.1,
      "text": "Ferry wind, if it comes, let it find the tired ones."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.1,
      "end": 22.52,
      "text": "Loose rope, open palm, no one punished for the calm."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.82,
      "end": 32.28,
      "text": "By morning we had patched the seam with sail cloth jokes and coffee steam."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.58,
      "end": 37.68,
      "text": "The child didn't aim the battered bow, probably fine and careful strokes."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.8,
      "end": 42.58,
      "text": "We laughed because it might be true, the kind of truth that lends with you."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.58,
      "end": 47.86,
      "text": "Not brave enough to aim to flag, but strong enough to mend a bag."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.06,
      "end": 52.96,
      "text": "The old scarf tried along the rail, the fishers argued with the sail."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.24,
      "end": 58.04,
      "text": "The wind came shy then came again like someone learning how to mend."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.56,
      "end": 64.74,
      "text": "It doesn't have to roll to move, it doesn't have to ask for proof or kinder weather."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.28,
      "end": 68.74,
      "text": "When it starts still has to pass through guarded hearts."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.54,
      "end": 75.96,
      "text": "If the fair wind finds us, let it find us as we are."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.26,
      "end": 81.86,
      "text": "Salted in every sleeve cup splinters in the sport."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.48,
      "end": 86.36,
      "text": "If the fair wind carries, let it carry without doubt."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.56,
      "end": 92.9,
      "text": "Not every good thing coming needs a storm to earn it first."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.8,
      "end": 102.64,
      "text": "We shared the bread and uneven parts, one kept crusting on kept hearts."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.94,
      "end": 107.68,
      "text": "Someone hung a crooked tune, the deck kept time with healing spoon."
    },
    {
      "start": 107.96,
      "end": 113.42,
      "text": "I thought of every bitter cup, every tide I drank and offended."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.98,
      "end": 118.32,
      "text": "No curse, they hungry for mistaken, first for mercy."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.32,
      "end": 121.66,
      "text": "The sea stayed sea, the robstay of the sky."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.98,
      "end": 129.62,
      "text": "They know a apology, but there was warmth along the planks and I let my soul proceed."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.78,
      "end": 137.44,
      "text": "It doesn't fix these behind, it doesn't make the old age kind."
    },
    {
      "start": 137.66,
      "end": 143.54,
      "text": "But joy can sit with so clear feet and still be joy and still be sweet."
